  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 14 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|C|=2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (-1)=6\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|B|$ are equal to $0.$",
